\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Problem Statement:\

\f1\b0\fs24 \
The Air pressure System is a critical component of a heavy duty vehicle that uses compressed air to force a piston to provide pressure to the brake pads, slowing the vehicle down. The benefits of using an APS instead of hydraulic system are the easy availability and long-term sustainability of natural air.\
\
This is a binary classification problem, in which +ve class indicates that a failure was caused by certain components of the APS, while -ve class indicates that the failure was caused by something else\
\
The checking of the APS of the system is expensive. Therefore we need to minimise this cost of servicing by using sensor data.\
\
\

\f0\b NOTE:
\f1\b0 \
False positives are alright to some extent but false negatives are very costly as if there is actually any problem in the APS system; it could eventually lead to fatal accidents.\
 }